     6	This is a starter template, not an app that ships. A criterion proves the
     7	**mechanism** is correct; it is not there to prove the *product* runs. So before
     8	writing one, ask: **would an adopter notice if this were missing?** If answering
     9	it needs a physical device, a custom CA, an Apple certificate, a reachable
    10	backend or store credentials, that answer belongs to the adopter's app, not to
    11	this repository - prove the mechanism at tier 1 or tier 2 here and hand the
    12	residual over. Precedent: koniz-dev/flutter-starter#48, #59, #62 and #108 each
    13	sat blocked for months of calendar time on exactly that (a real device, a custom
    14	CA, an Apple cert, on-device storage inspection) after the mechanism had already
    15	been proven, and all four closed with the residual assigned to the adopter.
